Q16:How would you refactor an existing trigger that has SOQL/DML inside loops in production?
A16: The 4 Rules for Safe Refactoring
Set & Map Accumulation: Loop once over Trigger.new to extract unique foreign keys (Set<Id>).
Single SOQL: Query with WHERE Id IN :idSet into a Map<Id, sObject>.
Map De-duplication for DML: If multiple children point to the same parent, storing updates in a Map<Id, SObject> prevents the runtime error: System.ListException: Duplicate id in list.
Database.insert(records, false): Using allOrNone = false ensures one invalid record doesn't block the entire 200-record batch, while capturing errors for observability.

Production Deployment Strategy
Deploy to Sandbox: Run a full bulk test with 200–500 records to verify governor limit usage via the Apex Execution Log (Limits.getQueries() and Limits.getDMLStatements()).
Feature Flag / Bypass: Deploy with a Custom Permission or Custom Metadata bypass switch so you can instantly fall back if unexpected regressions appear.
Off-Peak Deployment: Push during low-traffic windows to prevent database locks while active transactions touch the object.


