The Fix:
Virtual Scrolling / Pagination: Render only the visible viewport (e.g., 20–30 records) and dynamically load more as the user scrolls (infinite scroll) or paginate.
enable-infinite-loading in Datatable: Use lightning-datatable with infinite loading and onloadmore rather than loading all records into DOM memory.
Lazy DOM Instantiation: Use <template lwc:if={isVisible}> to defer rendering tabs, modals, accordions, and secondary cards until the user explicitly expands or clicks them.

b. eturning huge JSON payloads with unnecessary fields, nested relationships, and large unindexed data sets via @wire or imperative Apex.
only neccessary field should be queried, caching should be enabled .i.e. Cachable=true.

c.Modifying reactive @track properties or state variables inside getters, wire adapters, or loops triggers repeated reconciliation and 
re-rendering of the component's virtual DOM.
Avoid Complex Getters: Getters execute every time any reactive property in the component updates. Never put array operations (.filter(), .map(), .sort()), object cloning, or calculations inside getters—compute those once when data arrives and cache the result in a property.
Immutable Mutation Patterns: Avoid mutating deeply nested objects in loops. Clone and assign them once (this.data = [...updatedList]) so the LWC engine runs a single reconciliation cycle.

d. Third-Party Library Bloat & Static Resources
The Root Cause: Loading large external JS/CSS bundles (e.g., full Chart.js, D3.js, Leaflet) synchronously in renderedCallback() using loadScript on every render.
The Fix:
Load Once Guard: Always use a boolean guard (hasInitialized) so loadScript or loadStyle only executes once in the lifecycle.

